John H. wrote:

[roughly: NetHack items that have overwhelmingly
better replacements need to be given more "strategy"
reasons for their continued use throughout the
game.]

While I sympathize with your arguments, I don't
think someone playing NetHack completely unspoiled
would see the issues the same way you do at all.

You can play for _years_, unspoiled, before the
three kinds of plate mail look like the deathtraps
they are, and you stop cheering wildly the first
time you find plate mail. You can play pretty
much forever before thinking to wear and enchant
useless-looking dragon scales.

NetHack is full of lots of stuff that can be
eventually learned to be useless, but for the
unspoiled player, that learning process is all part
of the fun of the game.

I suspect what needs to be done to fix the current
situation is to warn new players better about the
joys of playing unspoiled, probably in the NetHack
Guidebook, rather than to make up for the
munchkinism of, say, the dragon armors by adding
munchkinism to all the other armors too.

I'm afraid nothing but an entirely new game and the
outlawing of spoiler writing would do much to fix
your issues for anyone reading rgrn.

